LINK 2: eta -> Omega_b  (standard BBN)
========================================================================

  Inputs:
    eta           = 6.1200e-10
    n_gamma       = 4.1073e+08 m^-3
    rho_crit      = 8.5327e-27 kg/m^3
    h             = 0.674

  Method 1 (direct n_B * m_p / rho_crit):
    n_B           = eta * n_gamma = 2.5137e-01 m^-3
    rho_b         = n_B * m_p = 4.2044e-28 kg/m^3
    Omega_b       = 0.0493

  Method 2 (BBN calibration Omega_b h^2 = 3.6515e-3 * eta_10):
    eta_10        = 6.12
    Omega_b h^2   = 0.022347
    Omega_b       = 0.0492

  Observed:  Omega_b = 0.0493

  [PASS] BBN Omega_b matches observation
         Omega_b(BBN) = 0.0492, obs = 0.0493, err = 0.2%
  [INFO] BBN is standard physics, zero free parameters given eta

